<item><title>Sierra Leone regulator reports NLE 7.4 million in 2024 revenue</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-regulator-reports-nle-7-4-million-in-2024-333409/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-regulator-reports-nle-7-4-million-in-2024-333409/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>The electricity and water watchdog collected the money from levies and licenses, up from NLE 2.3 million in 2023.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:36:22 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-regulator-reports-nle-7-4-million-in-2024-333409/share.jpg" length="41494" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-regulator-reports-nle-7-4-million-in-2024-333409/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Sierra Leone analysis questions vice president’s path to presidency</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-analysis-questions-vice-president-s-path-to-b42fab/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-analysis-questions-vice-president-s-path-to-b42fab/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>A political economist argues the office has often lacked a clear succession route, citing Solomon Ekuma Berewa’s 2007 election defeat.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:36:22 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" length="34790" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Sierra Leone charcoal trade sustains burners as tree loss threatens food security</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-charcoal-trade-sustains-burners-as-tree-loss-a237a3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-charcoal-trade-sustains-burners-as-tree-loss-a237a3/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>A 65-year-old burner says his family depends on the work, while the environmental agency warns that economic trees are being cut.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:36:22 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-charcoal-trade-sustains-burners-as-tree-loss-a237a3/share.jpg" length="43506" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-charcoal-trade-sustains-burners-as-tree-loss-a237a3/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Saudi ambassador plans Sierra Leone visa centre for workers</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/saudi-ambassador-plans-sierra-leone-visa-centre-for-workers-1e2eb3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/saudi-ambassador-plans-sierra-leone-visa-centre-for-workers-1e2eb3/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>The proposed centre would handle visa applications and biometric services, while a training facility would prepare prospective workers for Saudi jobs.</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:35:08 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" length="34790" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
